35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The technicians are gone, but the glasshouse crew remains. I see a shift in capability. @Midori, does the central funding cover the new modelling posts?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, the computing hours are free, but animal-unit rates spiked. I need to see how this shifts the burden onto the awardee.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, the spectroscopy suite sat idle for eleven weeks. One engineer covers three institutes. The shared load is already breaking.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The repository migration cleared the backlog. Deposits now clear in weeks, not months. @Toshio, does that mean the final data handoff is no longer a bottleneck?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, the data handoff is faster, but the science itself stalled. I found mechanism-focused awards ending with questions unresolved.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Toshio, if the science stalls, it is because the hands are missing. I see the glasshouse crew is intact, but the technicians are gone.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Kenji, the idle spectroscopy suite is worrying. If the shared load is breaking, the grant cannot rely on those machines.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, exactly. The glasshouse is booked solid, but the spectroscopy suite is a ghost town. We cannot fund a project that depends on broken shared capacity.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, that is a critical distinction. The logistics are fixed, but the biology is not. I need to know if the stalled science was due to inherent complexity or just poor planning.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, it was inherent complexity. The field sites lost seasons to weather, while indoor work continued. I will check the station records to confirm the pattern.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Kenji, the glasshouse crew is intact, but the spectroscopy suite is idle. We must fund work the remaining hands can actually perform.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, I agree. The free computing hours are a relief, but the animal-unit costs are a new burden. We must fund work that fits the remaining staff.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, I agree. We need to pick a project that uses the glasshouse, not the broken spectroscopy suite. The data is clear.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, if field sites lose seasons to weather, that is a delay we cannot engineer away. I am looking for proposals that avoid that specific fragility.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The field data confirms it. Weather is a variable we cannot control. I will look for proposals that stay indoors and avoid that risk.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
